  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Will + verbo base** (sin to). Forma corta: **'ll**. Negativa: **won't** (will not).",
      "",
      "**Cuatro usos principales**",
      "",
      "1. **Decisión en el momento:** *The phone is ringing. — I'll get it.*",
      "2. **Ofrecimiento:** *I'll help you with the bags.*",
      "3. **Promesa:** *I promise I won't tell anyone.*",
      "4. **Predicción / opinión:** *I think it will rain. · It will probably be cold.*",
      "",
      "**Preguntas:** *Will you help me? — Yes, I will. / No, I won't.* (también es un pedido amable)",
      "",
      "**Con la opinión:** *I think …* · *I don't think …* (no *I think … won't*): *I don't think it will rain.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** nunca *will to* ni *will + verbo conjugado*: *I'll help* (no *I'll to help* ni *I'll helps*).",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *I'll* /aɪl/ · *won't* /wəʊnt/ (no se confunde con *want* /wɒnt/)."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I will to open the window.",
        "right": "I'll open the window.",
        "note": "Will no lleva to."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I think it won't rain.",
        "right": "I don't think it will rain.",
        "note": "En inglés se niega el verbo think."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
